{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Sarah died.</b> It is not the way of Scripture to write the death of a woman even though she is righteous, except through a particular matter — such as Sarah, Rachel, Deborah, Miriam. Sarah: because Abraham spent precious money to bury her and did not have second thoughts, and this is one of the ten trials. Rachel: to make known that she was buried outside the cave. Deborah: to make known why that place was called Allon-bacuth. Miriam: on account of the well that ceased when she died." "<b>In Kiryat Arba.</b> One may say: Scripture wrote the place of her death, unlike in the case of Abraham and the other matriarchs — because Abraham sent her there when he set out to go to Mount Moriah, so that she would not become aware of the Akedah, for he was staying in Be'er Sheva, as it is written: 'וישב אברהם בבאר שבע.' And one may say: when she fell ill, he brought her there because the air of Hebron is good, and when she heard the news of the Akedah she died. Therefore '<b>And Abraham came</b>' from Be'er Sheva '<b>to eulogize Sarah</b>,' and therefore he needed to acquire there a burial estate, for it was not his place of dwelling." "<b>In Kiryat Arba.</b> A city that a man whose name was Arba built, as it is written: 'קרית ארבע האדם הגדול בענקים.' Another interpretation: a city that four owners inherited one after another — first to the tribe of Judah, afterward to Caleb, afterward to the priests, and afterward to the Levites, as is found in the book of Joshua, Bereshit Rabbah. And it was a city of refuge, and therefore Caleb was given only its fields, as it is written: 'את שדה העיר ואת חצריה נתנו לכלב בן יפונה לאחוזתו' — chapter 'יש נוחלין.' <b>And Abraham came</b> — one may say: even if he came only from outside, it says ויבא, as in: 'ויבא הביתה לעשות מלאכתו.'" "<b>To eulogize Sarah and to weep for her.</b> Because he had no prepared place for burial."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:27.452114828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}